<h2 id="multi-session">7. Running more than one session at once</h2>
<p>Multiple concurrent sessions are fully supported — different clubs, different courts, or a first-half/second-half split. If the same player ends up enrolled in two sessions that meet the same day of week with overlapping dates, that's flagged for you as a risk the moment you save the roster. It's a warning only — the scheduler doesn't automatically prevent it — so it's worth actually checking whether the two schedules end up colliding once both are generated. If a player really does end up double-booked, it's flagged everywhere: the session detail page, dashboard, Status page, and — just as importantly — directly to the player themselves on their own schedule, PDF, and calendar, so they can sort it out (request a sub or a swap) without needing you to catch it first.</p>

<h2 id="wrapping-up">8. Wrapping up a session</h2>
<p>Once a session's over, <strong>Archive</strong> it from the session detail page — this hides it from the dashboard and every player-facing page and stops all further reminder emails, without deleting anything; you can always unarchive it later to look something up. If a session was only ever test/dummy data, <strong>Delete</strong> it instead from the Edit page (permanent, with confirmation) — this never deletes the players themselves, since they're shared across sessions.</p>

